From: Alejandro Hernandez <alejandro@enedino.org>
Subject: [PATCH] newvers: support GNU date for SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

The supported Linux cross-build runs with GNU date. Its -r option reads
a reference file instead of converting an epoch timestamp, so a valid
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH supplied by OE fails kernel and loader version generation.
Try GNU date's equivalent after the native BSD invocation, preserving UTC,
and retain the error for values that neither implementation accepts.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/stand/common/newvers.sh
+++ b/stand/common/newvers.sh
@@ -45,7 +45,8 @@
 LC_ALL=C; export LC_ALL
 u=${USER-root} h=${HOSTNAME-`hostname`}
 if [ -n "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" ]; then
-	if ! t=$(date -ur $SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH 2>/dev/null); then
+	if ! t=$(date -ur "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" 2>/dev/null) &&
+	    ! t=$(date -u -d "@$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" 2>/dev/null); then
 		echo "Invalid SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" >&2
 		exit 1
 	fi
--- a/sys/conf/newvers.sh
+++ b/sys/conf/newvers.sh
@@ -196,7 +196,8 @@
 d=$builddir
 h=${HOSTNAME:-$(hostname)}
 if [ -n "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" ]; then
-	if ! t=$(date -ur $SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH 2>/dev/null); then
+	if ! t=$(date -ur "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" 2>/dev/null) &&
+	    ! t=$(date -u -d "@$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" 2>/dev/null); then
 		echo "Invalid SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" >&2
 		exit 1
 	fi
